From 460d117fb01b9eb16e49c926ed765d593bb8f050 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:57:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 084/118] sniff: log the stack of a panicking sniffer once a
 minute, not per connection

A sniffer that panics is recovered, and the error returned carried the whole stack in its
text. The router logged it at the error level for every connection, and the same text
stayed in the metadata of the connection, which the trackers keep for the live and the
last thousand closed connections. A client repeating the input that trips a sniffer bug
got a stack of several kilobytes per connection into the log.

The panic is now a SnifferPanicError: its text is one line, the stack is a field, and
errors.Is still finds ErrSnifferPanicked. The router logs the stack for the first panic
and then at most once a minute, with the number of panics in between, which are left to
the debug level; it drops the stack from the error once it has seen it, so the metadata
keeps the short text only.
